# Inkling-2-Mini (thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini, Inkling2LoopForConditionalGeneration) on TWO
# gfx1030 cards (V620, 29.98 GiB each), TP=2: the model's full 1,048,576-token context with
# FULL_AND_PIECEWISE HIP graphs, prefix caching and images. Attention shards by KV-head group, the
# MoE intermediate is split, lm_head / embedding are vocab-sharded, and the two all-reduces per
# layer visit run on the one-shot HIP all-reduce (rdna_ar) inside the graphs. Serving guide,
# switches, limits and the measured tables: docs/rdna2/inkling2-serving.md.
#
#   bash tools/rdna/serve_rdna.sh RECIPE=inkling2-mini-tp2 MODEL=/path/to/inkling2-mini \
#     VENV=/path/to/venv HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=4,5
#
# Override any key after RECIPE= or in the caller's environment (both win over this file), e.g.
#   bash tools/rdna/serve_rdna.sh RECIPE=inkling2-mini-tp2 SEQS=4                 # fewer graphs
#   bash tools/rdna/serve_rdna.sh RECIPE=inkling2-mini-tp2 VLLM_KV_CACHE_MARGIN_FLOOR_MIB=   # default 3 GiB floor
#
# Decode ms per token of one request (graph replay, 4,096-token engine; b requests at once):
#   b = 1 14.1, 2 16.2, 4 20.0, 8 25.9 (eager: 16.0, 17.5, 21.2, 27.1). Prompts of 261,052 /
#   942,628 / 1,046,914 tokens (1,048,576-token engine, this recipe) prefill at 811 / 378 / 349 tok/s
#   (the last takes 50.0 min) and decode at 24.4 / 49.8 / 54.3 ms/token at that depth, needles found.
# Memory per rank: weights 9.6 GiB with the vision tower (9.0 text only), KV 16 KiB per token
# (a 1,048,576-token request needs 16.1 GiB), the graphs 0.19 GiB. The engine keeps a margin of
# 3 GiB on ROCm beyond its measured activation peak (KV_CACHE_MARGIN_FLOOR_BYTES); with that floor
# the whole context is refused once graphs are captured (15.95 GiB of cache against 16.13 GiB at
# 184 tokens per step; docs/rdna2/inkling2-serving.md, "Long context"), so this recipe lowers the
# floor to 2 GiB (VLLM_KV_CACHE_MARGIN_FLOOR_MIB): the pool holds 1,062,736 tokens with the tower
# and the device peaked at 27.20 GiB of 29.98 during prompts of 261,052, 942,628 and 1,046,914 tokens.
# MAXBAT stays at
# 184 tokens per step, the chunk of those runs.
#
# DSpark speculative decoding has its own recipe, RECIPE=inkling2-mini-tp2-dspark (this recipe
# with SEQS 2, MAXLEN 780000 and the draft; docs/rdna2/inkling2-dspark.md): the model's own draft
# proposes 7 tokens and the engine verifies 2 per step for one or two requests, none above.
# Decode ms per token of one request, no draft -> K = 2 (SEQS 2, same cards): b = 1 14.0 -> 10.9
# (1.29x), 2 16.2 -> 14.2 (1.14x). The draft does not leave the full context its room: its
# full-attention layer keeps K/V on every rank (4 KiB per token, 4.05 GiB at 1,048,576 tokens) and
# its weights (0.8 GiB) and graphs come on top, so a 1,048,576-token request needs 20.18 GiB
# against the 16.14 GiB the engine has. The longest context is about 790,000 tokens at SEQS 2
# (780,000 booted: 790,494 tokens of KV) and 737,088 at SEQS 8:
#   bash tools/rdna/serve_rdna.sh RECIPE=inkling2-mini-tp2-dspark MODEL=/path/to/inkling2-mini \
#     VENV=/path/to/venv HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=4,5

SERVE_ENTRY=cli
SERVED_NAME=inkling2-mini
PORT=18222
TP=2
HOST=127.0.0.1

MTP=0
ATTN=none
EAGER=0
CG_MODE=FULL_AND_PIECEWISE
CG_CAPTURE_SIZES=0
MAXLEN=1048576
SEQS=8
MAXBAT=184
KV=auto
GMEM=0.92
RDNA_AR=1
FEATURES="prefix-caching"
EXTRA_ARGS='--limit-mm-per-prompt {"image":1}'

# --- RDNA vLLM env block ---
TUNABLEOP=0
# Floor of the headroom the KV sizing keeps free beyond its measured transient peak, in MiB
# (unset: 3 GiB on ROCm). Set empty to restore the engine default (the context then shrinks).
VLLM_KV_CACHE_MARGIN_FLOOR_MIB=2048
# One-shot all-reduce up to 256 KiB, RCCL above: a decode step reduces 2304 values per token
# (fp32 after the attention output projection, 9 KiB; fp16 after the MoE, 4.5 KiB), so up to 28
# tokens stay on the one-shot path; prefill chunks (184 tokens: 1.6 MiB) go to RCCL.
VLLM_FORCE_CUSTOM_ALL_REDUCE=0
VLLM_RDNA_AR_MAX_KB=256
VLLM_RDNA_AR_ONESHOT_KB=256
OMP_NUM_THREADS=8
TOKENIZERS_PARALLELISM=false
PYTHONFAULTHANDLER=1
